# Source: Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions,
# ch. 5, pp. 250–253. Mechanical effects are counterfactual abstractions.
title: <span class="term term-mossadegh">Mohammad Mossadegh</span>
new-page: true
is-pinned-card: true
tags: advisor
view-if: advisor_mossadegh_available = 1 and advisor_mossadegh_active = 1

= {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mohammad Mossadegh{!</span>!}

[? if front_formed = 0 and attempt_emergency_seen = 0: {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}
is an independent constitutional leader rather than the head of a common
opposition organization.
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} figures
and other politicians may consult him without surrendering their separate
positions. ?]
[? if front_formed = 0 and attempt_emergency_seen = 1: {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}
has been confined to his estates during the emergency. His constitutional
authority remains important; consultation now runs through correspondence and
intermediaries rather than a common headquarters. ?]
[? if front_formed = 1: {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}
is the central coordinating figure in the electoral protest that brought the
opposition coalition together. His intervention can help settle an immediate
question, but it cannot erase the coalition's differences. ?]

- @constitutional_case
- @hear_tendencies
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@constitutional_case
title: State the constitutional case
subtitle: <span class="term term-mossadegh">Mossadegh</span> gives aligned constitutionalists a formula they can repeat without pretending to share a full program
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; constitutional_legitimacy += 3; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 2; mossadegh_authority += 1; iran_party_relation += 2; common_resolution_timer = 0

{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!} restates the case
for representative institutions and constitutional government, then tests each
part of the argument against the procedure he expects the
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} to follow.

[? if front_formed = 0:
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} figures
and independent constitutionalists leave with a common case they can repeat
without claiming to belong to one organization or to have resolved their wider
disagreements. ?]
[? if front_formed = 1: The coalition leaves with a case its different
components can repeat without claiming that
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!} has resolved
their wider disagreements. ?]

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@hear_tendencies
title: Hear the coalition's competing tendencies
subtitle: Each tendency is heard in its own language; agreement is postponed rather than forced
view-if: front_formed = 1
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; coalition_meeting_timer = 0; iran_party_relation += 1; toilers_relation += 1; independent_nationalists_relation += 1; religious_network_relation += 1; iran_party_dissent -= 1; toilers_dissent -= 1; independent_nationalists_dissent -= 1; religious_network_dissent -= 1

The discussion does not produce agreement, but it clarifies what the
cooperating circles expect from the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}.
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!} asks each tendency to
state the boundary it cannot cross and the narrower action it can support.

Participants are less likely to mistake consultation for an attempt to absorb
them, and working relations improve across the coalition.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing
